From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:44:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] appxdeploymentclient: answer the package queries instead of
 returning E_NOTIMPL.

Office's Click-to-Run LASTRUN step integrates its MSIX add-ons.  It asks the
PackageManager whether Microsoft.WritingAssistant and Microsoft.Outlook.UriHandler
are installed, builds a Uri to OPushUtil.msix, tries to activate
Windows.Management.Deployment.StagePackageOptions, and when that class is not
registered falls back to IPackageManager6::ProvisionPackageForAllUsersAsync.

Every one of those failed here, and the last one killed the process:

  fixme:appx:package_manager_FindPackagesByPackageFamilyName ... stub
  err:combase:RoGetActivationFactory Failed to find library for
      L"Windows.Management.Deployment.StagePackageOptions"
  fixme:appx:package_manager_QueryInterface {0847e909-...} not implemented
  wine: Unhandled page fault on read access to 0000000000000000
        at address 000000014075707C

  14075706b: call [rip+0x8774f]      ; QueryInterface, returns E_NOINTERFACE
  140757071: mov rcx,[rbp+0x28]      ; the [out] it never wrote, still NULL
  14075707c: mov rax,[rcx]           ; fault
  140757086: mov rax,[rax+0x30]      ; slot 6: ProvisionPackageForAllUsersAsync

C2R is not being careless in a way Windows would punish: on Windows the QI
succeeds, the call returns an operation, and the operation reports whether the
deployment worked.  The stubs here break that contract -- they return E_NOTIMPL
and leave the [out] parameter exactly as the caller left it -- so the caller
dereferences a pointer nobody wrote.  The scenario then stays EXECUTING and the
install never finishes.

So answer the questions rather than declining them.  Wine has no AppX package
store: no package is registered, and none can be deployed.  Both of those have
a truthful WinRT answer.

  - FindPackages* hand back an empty IIterable<Package>.  Zero packages match,
    because zero packages exist.
  - FindPackageBy*FullName report S_OK with a NULL package, which is what a
    lookup that finds nothing returns.
  - every *Async returns an operation that has already reached
    AsyncStatus_Error, with ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED in IAsyncInfo::ErrorCode and a
    DeploymentResult carrying the same code and an ErrorText saying no package
    was deployed.  GetResults still yields that result, the way Microsoft's own
    deployment samples read the reason for a failure.  A caller learns the
    deployment did not happen however it chooses to look.
  - the remaining stubs at least NULL their [out] parameters, so the next
    caller that skips the HRESULT finds a NULL rather than whatever was on its
    stack.

IPackageManager6 is implemented alongside, from the SDK IDL: uuid
0847e909-53cd-4e4f-832e-57d180f6e447, six methods, and the
AddPackageByAppInstallerOptions enum and PackageVolume runtime class its
signatures need.

appxprobe walks the same path C2R does and now reports QI IPackageManager6 0x0,
an empty but walkable package collection, status Error with code 0x80070032, the
completed handler invoked exactly once, and a DeploymentResult with a matching
ExtendedErrorCode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 984dba990b1537779e3608389c98e6dfa47f3c37)

diff --git a/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/Makefile.in b/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/Makefile.in
index 315f501d9cd..f07553b9c1b 100644
--- a/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/Makefile.in
@@ -3,5 +3,6 @@ IMPORTS = combase
 
 SOURCES = \
 	classes.idl \
+	deployment.c \
 	main.c \
 	package.c
diff --git a/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/deployment.c b/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/deployment.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..f300dbfa92a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/appxdeploymentclient/deployment.c
@@ -0,0 +1,773 @@
+/* WinRT Windows.Management.Deployment deployment results
+ *
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 AltarsCN
+ *
